## 6. Environment Variables (names only — values never committed)

`PORT`, `MONGO_URI`, `JWT_SECRET`, `JWT_REFRESH_SECRET`, `JWT_EXPIRE`,
`JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRE`, `NODE_ENV`, `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID`, `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET`,
`GROK_KEY` (unused?)

Required for new code to run: at minimum `MONGO_URI`, `JWT_SECRET`, `JWT_REFRESH_SECRET`.

---

## 7. Notes for Future Work

- User's uncommitted working-tree changes must not be discarded when refactoring auth/payment.
- If live Razorpay keys exist in `rzp-key.csv`, rotate them immediately.
- Decide and document the intended access model for `/api/coding` (public vs premium).
- Add a test runner (Jest or Vitest) before making any of the critical fixes — auth and
  scoring paths need regression coverage.
- When fixing CORS, confirm the exact frontend origin(s) first (Vercel preview URLs vs prod).
